File: EdgeIdeals.info, Node: cliqueNumber, Next: complementGraph, Prev: cliqueComplex, Up: Top

cliqueNumber -- computes the clique number of a graph
*****************************************************

  * Usage: 
        c = cliqueNumber G
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note graph: Graph,, 
  * Outputs:
      * c, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the clique number of G

Description
===========

cliqueNumber returns the clique number of a graph, the size of the largest
clique contained in the graph.  This number is also related to the dimension of
the clique complex of the graph.

+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..d];                                     |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : cliqueNumber completeGraph R                      |
|                                                       |
|o2 = 4                                                 |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : G = graph({a*b,b*c,a*c,a*d})                      |
|                                                       |
|o3 = Graph{"edges" => {{a, b}, {a, c}, {b, c}, {a, d}}}|
|           "ring" => R                                 |
|           "vertices" => {a, b, c, d}                  |
|                                                       |
|o3 : Graph                                             |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : cliqueNumber G                                    |
|                                                       |
|o4 = 3                                                 |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : dim cliqueComplex G + 1 == cliqueNumber G         |
|                                                       |
|o5 = true                                              |
+-------------------------------------------------------+

