connectedComponents -- returns the connected components of a hypergraph
***********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        L = connectedComponents H
  * Inputs:
      * H, a *note hypergraph: HyperGraph,, 
  * Outputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of lists of vertices. Each list
        of vertices is a connected component of H.

Description
===========

This function returns the connected components of a hypergraph. A connected
component of a hypergraph is any maximal set of vertices which are pairwise
connected by a non-trivial path. Isolated vertices, which are those not
appearing in any edge, do not appear in any connected components. This is in
contrast to *note connectedGraphComponents: connectedGraphComponents, in which
isolated vertices form their own connected components. See the *note Connected
Components Tutorial: Connected Components Tutorial, for more information.



+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..l];                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : H = hyperGraph {a*b*c, c*d, d*e*f, h*i, i*j, l}                         |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = HyperGraph{"edges" => {{a, b, c}, {c, d}, {d, e, f}, {h, i}, {i, j},    |
|                "ring" => R                                                  |
|                "vertices" => {a, b, c, d, e, f, g, h, i, j, k, l}           |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : HyperGraph                                                              |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|{l}}}                                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : L = connectedComponents H                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = {{a, b, c, d, e, f}, {h, i, j}, {l}}                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : apply(L, C -> inducedHyperGraph(H,C))                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = {HyperGraph{"edges" => {{a, b, c}, {c, d}, {d, e, f}}},                 |
|                 "ring" => QQ[a..f]                                          |
|                 "vertices" => {a, b, c, d, e, f}                            |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     HyperGraph{"edges" => {{h, i}, {i, j}}}, HyperGraph{"edges" => {{l}} }} |
|                "ring" => QQ[h..j]                       "ring" => QQ[l]     |
|                "vertices" => {h, i, j}                  "vertices" => {l}   |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

In the following example, hypergraph H contains the isolated vertex d and the
vertex c which is in an edge of size one. Notice that d does not appear in any
connected component while c does.



+-------------------------------------------+
|i5 : R = QQ[a,b,c,d];                      |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i6 : H = hyperGraph {a*b, c}               |
|                                           |
|o6 = HyperGraph{"edges" => {{a, b}, {c}}  }|
|                "ring" => R                |
|                "vertices" => {a, b, c, d} |
|                                           |
|o6 : HyperGraph                            |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i7 : connectedComponents H                 |
|                                           |
|o7 = {{a, b}, {c}}                         |
|                                           |
|o7 : List                                  |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i8 : isolatedVertices H                    |
|                                           |
|o8 = {d}                                   |
|                                           |
|o8 : List                                  |
+-------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note Connected Components Tutorial: Connected Components Tutorial, --
    clarifying the difference between graph and hypergraph components
  * *note connectedGraphComponents: connectedGraphComponents, -- returns the
    connected components of a graph
  * *note isConnected: isConnected, -- determines if a (hyper)graph is
    connected
  * *note numConnectedComponents: numConnectedComponents, -- returns the number
    of connected components in a (hyper)graph
  * *note isolatedVertices: isolatedVertices, -- returns all vertices not
    contained in any edge

Ways to use connectedComponents:
================================

  * "connectedComponents(HyperGraph)"
  * *note connectedComponents(SimplicialComplex):
    (SimplicialComplexes)connectedComponents_lpSimplicialComplex_rp, -- find
    the connected components of an abstract simplicial complex

For the programmer
==================

The object *note connectedComponents:
(SimplicialComplexes)connectedComponents_lpSimplicialComplex_rp, is a *note
method function: (Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

