connectedGraphComponents -- returns the connected components of a graph
***********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        L = connectedGraphComponents G
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note hypergraph: HyperGraph,, 
  * Outputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of lists of vertices. Each list
        of vertices is a connected component of G.

Description
===========

This function returns the connected components of a graph. A connected
component of a graph is any maximal set of vertices which are pairwise
connected by a (possibly trivial) path. Isolated vertices, which are those not
appearing in any edge, form their own connected components. This is in contrast
to *note connectedComponents:
(SimplicialComplexes)connectedComponents_lpSimplicialComplex_rp, in which
isolated vertices do not appear in any connected components. See the *note
Connected Components Tutorial: Connected Components Tutorial, for more
information.



+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..k];                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : G = graph {a*b,b*c,c*d,a*d,f*g,h*i,j*k,h*k}                             |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = Graph{"edges" => {{a, b}, {b, c}, {a, d}, {c, d}, {f, g}, {h, i}, {h,   |
|           "ring" => R                                                       |
|           "vertices" => {a, b, c, d, e, f, g, h, i, j, k}                   |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Graph                                                                   |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|k}, {j, k}}}                                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : L = connectedGraphComponents G                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = {{e}, {a, b, c, d}, {f, g}, {h, i, j, k}}                               |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

In the following example, graph G contains the isolated vertex d. Notice that d
appears in its own connected component and hence G is not connected.



+---------------------------------------+
|i4 : R = QQ[a,b,c,d];                  |
+---------------------------------------+
|i5 : G = graph {a*b, b*c}              |
|                                       |
|o5 = Graph{"edges" => {{a, b}, {b, c}}}|
|           "ring" => R                 |
|           "vertices" => {a, b, c, d}  |
|                                       |
|o5 : Graph                             |
+---------------------------------------+
|i6 : connectedGraphComponents G        |
|                                       |
|o6 = {{d}, {a, b, c}}                  |
|                                       |
|o6 : List                              |
+---------------------------------------+
|i7 : isolatedVertices G                |
|                                       |
|o7 = {d}                               |
|                                       |
|o7 : List                              |
+---------------------------------------+
|i8 : isConnectedGraph G                |
|                                       |
|o8 = false                             |
+---------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note Connected Components Tutorial: Connected Components Tutorial, --
    clarifying the difference between graph and hypergraph components
  * *note connectedComponents:
    (SimplicialComplexes)connectedComponents_lpSimplicialComplex_rp, -- find
    the connected components of an abstract simplicial complex
  * *note isConnectedGraph: isConnectedGraph, -- determines if a graph is
    connected
  * *note numConnectedGraphComponents: numConnectedGraphComponents, -- returns
    the number of connected components in a graph
  * *note isolatedVertices: isolatedVertices, -- returns all vertices not
    contained in any edge

