getCliques -- returns cliques in a graph
****************************************

  * Usage: 
        C = getCliques(G,d)
        C = getCliques G
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note graph: Graph,, 
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, representing the size of the
        cliques desired
  * Outputs:
      * C, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of cliques of size d or, if no d
        is entered, all cliques

Description
===========

A clique of a graph is a subset of its vertices which induces a complete
subgraph. That is, a set of vertices is a clique if every pair of vertices in
the set forms an edge of the graph. This function returns all cliques of a
specified size, and if no size is given, it returns all cliques.  Note that all
the edges of the graph are considered cliques of size two.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..d];                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : G = completeGraph R                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = Graph{"edges" => {{a, b}, {a, c}, {a, d}, {b, c}, {b, d}, {c, d}}}      |
|           "ring" => R                                                       |
|           "vertices" => {a, b, c, d}                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Graph                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : getCliques(G,3)                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = {{a, b, c}, {a, b, d}, {a, c, d}, {b, c, d}}                            |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : getCliques(G,4)                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = {{a, b, c, d}}                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : getCliques G                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = {{a, b}, {a, c}, {b, c}, {a, d}, {b, d}, {c, d}, {a, b, c}, {a, b, d},  |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     {a, c, d}, {b, c, d}, {a, b, c, d}}                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note cliqueNumber: cliqueNumber, -- computes the clique number of a graph

Ways to use getCliques:
=======================

  * "getCliques(Graph)"
  * "getCliques(Graph,ZZ)"

