Graph -- a class for graphs
***************************

Description
===========

This class represents simple graphs. This class extends *note HyperGraph:
HyperGraph, and hence inherits all HyperGraph methods.

+---------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[w,x,y,z];                        |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i2 : G = graph(R, {{w,x},{w,y},{w,z},{y,z}});|
+---------------------------------------------+
|i3 : vertices G                              |
|                                             |
|o3 = {w, x, y, z}                            |
|                                             |
|o3 : List                                    |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i4 : edges G                                 |
|                                             |
|o4 = {{w, x}, {w, y}, {w, z}, {y, z}}        |
|                                             |
|o4 : List                                    |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i5 : ring G                                  |
|                                             |
|o5 = R                                       |
|                                             |
|o5 : PolynomialRing                          |
+---------------------------------------------+

Like hypergraphs, graphs are associated with a polynomial ring whose variables
are the vertices of the graph. Isolated vertices should not appear in the edge
list. As a consequence, the *note edgeIdeal: edgeIdeal, of a graph is always
generated by quadratics. The fact that isolated vertices are not edges in a
graph affects the output of the methods *note connectedComponents:
(SimplicialComplexes)connectedComponents_lpSimplicialComplex_rp,, *note
numConnectedComponents: numConnectedComponents,, and *note isConnected:
isConnected,. One can use *note connectedGraphComponents:
connectedGraphComponents,, *note numConnectedGraphComponents:
numConnectedGraphComponents,, and *note isConnectedGraph: isConnectedGraph, to
ensure that each isolated vertex is counted as a separate connected component.

