HyperGraph -- a class for hypergraphs
*************************************

Description
===========

This class represents hypergraphs. A hypergraph is a tuple (V,E) of vertices V
and edges E which are subsets of the vertices. In this package, all hypergraphs
have the additional property that no edge is a subset of any other edge.
Hypergraphs of this form are often referred to as clutters.

+------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[w,x,y,z];                           |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : H = hyperGraph(R, {{w,x},{w,y,z},{x,y,z}});|
+------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : vertices H                                 |
|                                                |
|o3 = {w, x, y, z}                               |
|                                                |
|o3 : List                                       |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : edges H                                    |
|                                                |
|o4 = {{w, x}, {w, y, z}, {x, y, z}}             |
|                                                |
|o4 : List                                       |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : ring H                                     |
|                                                |
|o5 = R                                          |
|                                                |
|o5 : PolynomialRing                             |
+------------------------------------------------+

Hypergraphs are always associated with a polynomial ring whose variables are
the vertices of the hypergraph.

