inducedGraph -- returns the induced subgraph of a graph
*******************************************************

  * Usage: 
        h = inducedGraph(G, L)
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note graph: Graph,, 
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of vertices (i.e. variables in
        the ring of G)
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note OriginalRing: inducedGraph_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmOriginalRing=>_pd_pd_pd_
        rp, => ..., default value false, use OriginalRing inside inducedGraph
        or inducedHyperGraph
  * Outputs:
      * h, a *note graph: Graph,, the induced subgraph of G whose edges are
        contained in L

Description
===========

This function returns the induced subgraph of a graph on a specified set of
vertices. This function enables the user to create subgraphs of the original
graph. inducedGraph accepts a *note Graph: Graph, as input and returns a *note
Graph: Graph, as well. Use *note inducedHyperGraph: inducedHyperGraph, for a
*note HyperGraph: HyperGraph, instead.

The default option is for the ring of the induced subgraph to contain only
variables in L. Then the current ring must be changed before working with the
induced subgraph. We use this setup to avoid having a lot of isolated vertices
in the induced graph. However, one can set the option *note OriginalRing:
OriginalRing, to true if one wants to give the induced graph the same ring as
the original graph.



+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a,b,c,d,e];                                                  |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : G = graph {a*b,b*c,c*d,d*e,e*a} -- graph of the 5-cycle             |
|                                                                         |
|o2 = Graph{"edges" => {{a, b}, {b, c}, {c, d}, {a, e}, {d, e}}}          |
|           "ring" => R                                                   |
|           "vertices" => {a, b, c, d, e}                                 |
|                                                                         |
|o2 : Graph                                                               |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : H1 = inducedGraph(G,{b,c,d,e})                                      |
|                                                                         |
|o3 = Graph{"edges" => {{b, c}, {c, d}, {d, e}}}                          |
|           "ring" => QQ[b..e]                                            |
|           "vertices" => {b, c, d, e}                                    |
|                                                                         |
|o3 : Graph                                                               |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : H2 = inducedGraph(G,{a,b,d,e})                                      |
|                                                                         |
|o4 = Graph{"edges" => {{a, b}, {a, e}, {d, e}}}                          |
|           "ring" => QQ[a..b, d..e]                                      |
|           "vertices" => {a, b, d, e}                                    |
|                                                                         |
|o4 : Graph                                                               |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : use ring H1                                                         |
|                                                                         |
|o5 = QQ[b..e]                                                            |
|                                                                         |
|o5 : PolynomialRing                                                      |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : inducedGraph(H1,{c,d,e})                                            |
|                                                                         |
|o6 = Graph{"edges" => {{c, d}, {d, e}}}                                  |
|           "ring" => QQ[c..e]                                            |
|           "vertices" => {c, d, e}                                       |
|                                                                         |
|o6 : Graph                                                               |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : use ring G                                                          |
|                                                                         |
|o7 = R                                                                   |
|                                                                         |
|o7 : PolynomialRing                                                      |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : inducedGraph(G,{b,c,d,e},OriginalRing=>true) --H1 but in bigger ring|
|                                                                         |
|o8 = Graph{"edges" => {{b, c}, {c, d}, {d, e}}}                          |
|           "ring" => R                                                   |
|           "vertices" => {a, b, c, d, e}                                 |
|                                                                         |
|o8 : Graph                                                               |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Equivalently, one can use *note changeRing: changeRing, (and *note graph:
graph,) to move the induced graph back into the original ring.

+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : R = QQ[a,b,c,d,e];                                         |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : G = graph {a*b,b*c,c*d,d*e,e*a} -- graph of the 5-cycle   |
|                                                                |
|o10 = Graph{"edges" => {{a, b}, {b, c}, {c, d}, {a, e}, {d, e}}}|
|            "ring" => R                                         |
|            "vertices" => {a, b, c, d, e}                       |
|                                                                |
|o10 : Graph                                                     |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : H = inducedGraph(G,{b,c,d})                               |
|                                                                |
|o11 = Graph{"edges" => {{b, c}, {c, d}}}                        |
|            "ring" => QQ[b..d]                                  |
|            "vertices" => {b, c, d}                             |
|                                                                |
|o11 : Graph                                                     |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : graph changeRing(H,R,{b,c,d})                             |
|                                                                |
|o12 = Graph{"edges" => {{c, d}, {b, c}}  }                      |
|            "ring" => R                                         |
|            "vertices" => {a, b, c, d, e}                       |
|                                                                |
|o12 : Graph                                                     |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+

