        or inducedHyperGraph
  * Outputs:
      * h, a *note hypergraph: HyperGraph,, the induced subgraph of H whose
        edges are contained in L

Description
===========

This function returns the induced subgraph of a (hyper)graph on a specified set
of vertices. This function enables the user to create subgraphs of the original
(hyper)graph.

The default option is for the ring of the induced subgraph to contain only
variables in L. Then the current ring must be changed before working with the
induced subgraph. We use this setup to avoid having a lot of isolated vertices
in the induced (hyper)graph. However, one can set the option *note
OriginalRing: OriginalRing, to true if one wants to give the induced
(hyper)graph the same ring as the original (hyper)graph.

Note: Since *note Graph: Graph, is a *note Type: (Macaulay2Doc)Type, of *note
HyperGraph: HyperGraph,, inducedHyperGraph can be used for graphs, but the
output is a *note HyperGraph: HyperGraph,. If one prefers to have a graph
returned instead, use *note inducedGraph: inducedGraph,.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a,b,c,d,e];                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : G = graph {a*b,b*c,c*d,d*e,e*a} -- graph of the 5-cycle                 |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = Graph{"edges" => {{a, b}, {b, c}, {c, d}, {a, e}, {d, e}}}              |
