isConnected -- determines if a (hyper)graph is connected
********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        b = isConnected H
  * Inputs:
      * H, a *note hypergraph: HyperGraph,, 
  * Outputs:
      * b, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, true if H is
        connected, false otherwise

Description
===========

This function checks if the given (hyper)graph H is connected. A (hyper)graph
is said to be connected if it has exactly one connected component.

Isolated vertices do not count as connected components and will not make this
method return false. This is in contrast to *note isConnectedGraph:
isConnectedGraph, in which isolated vertices form their own connected
components. See the *note Connected Components Tutorial: Connected Components
Tutorial, for more information.



+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = QQ[a..e];                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : G = graph {a*b,b*c,c*d,d*e,a*e} -- the 5-cycle (connected)              |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = Graph{"edges" => {{a, b}, {b, c}, {c, d}, {a, e}, {d, e}}}              |
|           "ring" => S                                                       |
|           "vertices" => {a, b, c, d, e}                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Graph                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : H = graph {a*b,b*c,c*a,d*e} -- a 3-cycle and a disjoint edge (not       |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = Graph{"edges" => {{a, b}, {a, c}, {b, c}, {d, e}}}                      |
|           "ring" => S                                                       |
|           "vertices" => {a, b, c, d, e}                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : Graph                                                                   |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|connected)                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : isConnected G                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = true                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : isConnected H                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = false                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

In the following example, the graph G has the isolated vertex d. As d is not
considered to be in any connected component, this graph is connected.



+---------------------------------------+
|i6 : S = QQ[a,b,c,d];                  |
+---------------------------------------+
|i7 : G = graph {a*b,b*c}               |
|                                       |
|o7 = Graph{"edges" => {{a, b}, {b, c}}}|
|           "ring" => S                 |
|           "vertices" => {a, b, c, d}  |
|                                       |
|o7 : Graph                             |
+---------------------------------------+
|i8 : isolatedVertices G                |
|                                       |
|o8 = {d}                               |
|                                       |
|o8 : List                              |
+---------------------------------------+
|i9 : isConnected G                     |
|                                       |
|o9 = true                              |
+---------------------------------------+

