isGoodLeaf -- determines if an edge is a good leaf
**************************************************

  * Usage: 
        b = isGoodLeaf(H,n)
  * Inputs:
      * H, a *note hypergraph: HyperGraph,, 
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, index of an edge
  * Outputs:
      * b, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, true if edge n of H
        is a good leaf

Description
===========

A good leaf of hypergraph H is an edge L whose intersections with all other
edges form a totally ordered set. It follows that L must have a free vertex. In
the graph setting, a good leaf is an edge containing a vertex of degree one.
The notion of a good leaf was introduced by X. Zheng in her Ph.D. thesis
(2004).

+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..g];                                             |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : H = hyperGraph {a*b*c*d, b*c*d*e, c*d*f, d*g, e*f*g};     |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : edges(H)                                                  |
|                                                               |
|o3 = {{a, b, c, d}, {b, c, d, e}, {c, d, f}, {d, g}, {e, f, g}}|
|                                                               |
|o3 : List                                                      |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : isGoodLeaf(H,0)                                           |
|                                                               |
|o4 = true                                                      |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : isGoodLeaf(H,1)                                           |
|                                                               |
|o5 = false                                                     |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+

