neighbors -- returns the neighbors of a vertex or list of vertices
******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        N = neighbors(H,V)
        N = neighbors(H,n)
        N = neighbors(H,L)
  * Inputs:
      * H, a *note hypergraph: HyperGraph,, 
      * V, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a vertex
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the index of a vertex
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of vertices or indices of
        vertices
  * Outputs:
      * N, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of neighbors to the given vertex
        or vertices

Description
===========

The vertices adjacent to vertex V are called the neighbors of V. The neighbors
of a list of vertices L are those vertices that are not in L and are adjacent
to a vertex in L.

+-----------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..f];                       |
+-----------------------------------------+
