File: EdgeIdeals.info, Node: numConnectedComponents, Next: numConnectedGraphComponents, Prev: neighbors, Up: Top

numConnectedComponents -- returns the number of connected components in a (hyper)graph
**************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        d = numConnectedComponents H
  * Inputs:
      * H, a *note hypergraph: HyperGraph,, 
  * Outputs:
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the number of connected
        components of H

Description
===========

This function returns the number of connected components of a hypergraph. A
connected component of a hypergraph is any maximal set of vertices which are
pairwise connected by a non-trivial path.  Isolated vertices, which are those
not appearing in any edge, do not count as connected components. This is in
contrast to *note numConnectedGraphComponents: numConnectedGraphComponents, in
which isolated vertices are counted as connected components. See the *note
Connected Components Tutorial: Connected Components Tutorial, for more
information.

The algorithm used by numConnectedComponents turns H into a simplicial complex,
and then computes the rank of the 0^{th} reduced homology group. This number
plus 1 gives the number of connected components of H.

We depart from this method in two cases: We define the hypergraph with only the
empty edge (corresponding to the irrelevant simplicial complex) and the
hypergraph with empty edge set (corresponding to the void simplicial complex)
to have 0 connected components.

Although this method can be applied to graphs, its output does not match the
most common meaning for the number of connected components of a graph. Instead,
one should use *note numConnectedGraphComponents: numConnectedGraphComponents,.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = QQ[a..e];                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : g = graph {a*b,b*c,c*d,d*e,a*e} -- the 5-cycle (connected)              |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = Graph{"edges" => {{a, b}, {b, c}, {c, d}, {a, e}, {d, e}}}              |
|           "ring" => S                                                       |
|           "vertices" => {a, b, c, d, e}                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Graph                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : h = graph {a*b,b*c,c*a,d*e} -- a 3-cycle and a disjoint edge (not       |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = Graph{"edges" => {{a, b}, {a, c}, {b, c}, {d, e}}}                      |
|           "ring" => S                                                       |
|           "vertices" => {a, b, c, d, e}                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : Graph                                                                   |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|connected)                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : numConnectedComponents g                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = 1                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : numConnectedComponents h                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = 2                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

The following example contains a hypergraph with an edge of size one. The
vertex in this edge is not considered isolated and does count as a connected
component.

+-------------------------------------------+
|i6 : S = QQ[a..d];                         |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i7 : H = hyperGraph {a*b,c}                |
|                                           |
|o7 = HyperGraph{"edges" => {{a, b}, {c}}  }|
|                "ring" => S                |
|                "vertices" => {a, b, c, d} |
|                                           |
|o7 : HyperGraph                            |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i8 : isolatedVertices H                    |
|                                           |
|o8 = {d}                                   |
|                                           |
|o8 : List                                  |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i9 : connectedComponents H                 |
|                                           |
|o9 = {{a, b}, {c}}                         |
|                                           |
|o9 : List                                  |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i10 : numConnectedComponents H             |
|                                           |
|o10 = 2                                    |
+-------------------------------------------+

