File: EdgeIdeals.info, Node: randomHyperGraph_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmBranchLimit=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, Next: randomHyperGraph_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmTimeLimit=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, Prev: randomHyperGraph, Up: Top

randomHyperGraph(...,BranchLimit=>...) -- limit recursive branching in randomHyperGraph
***************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        G = randomHyperGraph(R,D,BranchLimit=>n)
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, number of branches at each
        level in the recursion of randomHyperGraph

Description
===========

The *note randomHyperGraph: randomHyperGraph, method follows a backtracking
algorithm to generate edges with no inclusions between them. At each step in
the recursive tree,  *note randomHyperGraph: randomHyperGraph, will make
BranchLimit attempts to complete its list of edges. Thus, if a hypergraph with
N edges is required, *note randomHyperGraph: randomHyperGraph, may take
BranchLimit^N steps before terminating. To be more precise, the method is
implemented so that it makes BranchLimit + L attempts at level L of the
recursion. The default value is 3.

See also
========

  * *note TimeLimit: TimeLimit, -- optional argument for randomHyperGraph
  * *note randomHyperGraph: randomHyperGraph, -- returns a random hypergraph

Functions with optional argument named BranchLimit:
===================================================

  * *note randomHyperGraph(...,BranchLimit=>...):
    randomHyperGraph_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmBranchLimit=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, -- limit
    recursive branching in randomHyperGraph

Further information
===================

  * Default value: 3
  * Function: *note randomHyperGraph: randomHyperGraph, -- returns a random
    hypergraph
  * Option key: *note BranchLimit: BranchLimit, -- optional argument for
    randomHyperGraph
