randomHyperGraph(...,TimeLimit=>...) -- limit the running time of randomHyperGraph
**********************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        randomHyperGraph(R,D,TimeLimit=>s)
  * Inputs:
      * s, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, time in seconds before
        randomHyperGraph returns null

Description
===========

The *note randomHyperGraph: randomHyperGraph, method follows a backtracking
algorithm to generate edges with no inclusions between them. As it may take a
long time to terminate, a time limit is imposed on the method. The TimeLimit
option is the amount of time, in seconds, that the method *note
randomHyperGraph: randomHyperGraph, will take before terminating. A value of 0
is interpreted as one day. The default value is 5 (seconds).

See also
========

