TimeLimit -- optional argument for randomHyperGraph
***************************************************

Description
===========

The *note randomHyperGraph: randomHyperGraph, method follows a backtracking
algorithm to generate edges with no inclusions between them. As it may take a
long time to terminate, a time limit is imposed on the method. The TimeLimit
option is the amount of time, in seconds, that the method *note
randomHyperGraph: randomHyperGraph, will take before terminating. A value of 0
is interpreted as one day. The default value is 5 (seconds).

See also
========

  * *note BranchLimit: BranchLimit, -- optional argument for randomHyperGraph
  * *note randomHyperGraph: randomHyperGraph, -- returns a random hypergraph

Functions with optional argument named TimeLimit:
=================================================

  * *note randomHyperGraph(...,TimeLimit=>...):
    randomHyperGraph_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmTimeLimit=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, -- limit the
    running time of randomHyperGraph

For the programmer
==================

The object *note TimeLimit: TimeLimit, is a *note symbol:
(Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,.

