File: EdgeIdeals.info, Node: vertexCovers, Next: vertices_lpHyperGraph_rp, Prev: vertexCoverNumber, Up: Top

vertexCovers -- list the minimal vertex covers of a (hyper)graph
****************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        c = vertexCovers(H)
  * Inputs:
      * H, a *note hypergraph: HyperGraph,, the input
  * Outputs:
      * c, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of the minimal vertex covers of
        H.  The vertex covers are represented as monomials.

Description
===========

This function returns the minimal vertex covers of a (hyper)graph. A vertex
cover is a subset of the vertices such that every edge of the (hyper)graph has
non-empty intersection with this set.  The minimal vertex covers are given by
the minimal generators of the cover ideal of H.

+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = QQ[a..d];                                                |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : g = graph {a*b,b*c,c*d,d*a} -- the four cycle                |
|                                                                  |
|o2 = Graph{"edges" => {{a, b}, {b, c}, {a, d}, {c, d}}}           |
|           "ring" => S                                            |
|           "vertices" => {a, b, c, d}                             |
|                                                                  |
|o2 : Graph                                                        |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : vertexCovers g                                               |
|                                                                  |
|o3 = {a*c, b*d}                                                   |
|                                                                  |
|o3 : List                                                         |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : coverIdeal g                                                 |
|                                                                  |
|o4 = monomialIdeal (a*c, b*d)                                     |
|                                                                  |
|o4 : MonomialIdeal of S                                           |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : flatten entries gens coverIdeal g == vertexCovers g          |
|                                                                  |
|o5 = true                                                         |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : S = QQ[a..e];                                                |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : h = hyperGraph {a*b*c,a*d,c*e,b*d*e}                         |
|                                                                  |
|o7 = HyperGraph{"edges" => {{a, b, c}, {a, d}, {c, e}, {b, d, e}}}|
|                "ring" => S                                       |
|                "vertices" => {a, b, c, d, e}                     |
|                                                                  |
|o7 : HyperGraph                                                   |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : vertexCovers(h)                                              |
|                                                                  |
|o8 = {a*b*c, c*d, a*e, b*d*e}                                     |
|                                                                  |
|o8 : List                                                         |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note coverIdeal: coverIdeal, -- creates the cover ideal of a (hyper)graph
  * *note vertexCoverNumber: vertexCoverNumber, -- find the vertex covering
    number of a (hyper)graph

Ways to use vertexCovers:
=========================

  * "vertexCovers(HyperGraph)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note vertexCovers: vertexCovers, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

